#import "/modern-iaf/manuals/layout/manual.typ": *

#idx("Training course, phase 7")#idx("Air-to-air")Phase 7, Air-to-air, is the seventh phase of each jet's course: five #term("lesson")s by day, one at night and check ride 7, each a full sortie from the jet's home base to a training area and back. The fights are the training fight against Red 1 (@training-fight). The briefing in the game gives the lesson's steps, and the jet's flight manual gives the weapons: the #other("f16i", "aa-weapons"), the #other("f16d", "aa-weapons") and the #other("f35i", "aa-weapons").

#grid-table(
  (auto, 1fr, 1fr),
  ([Lesson], [What it teaches], [How it is graded]),
  [7.1 Intercept a drone], [A radar intercept guided by the #term("AWACS"), and a live missile shot at each of two drones.], [Targets shot down; shots inside the missile's reach.],
  [7.2 BVR against aggressors], [The shot beyond visual range at an aggressor F-16 that shoots back, and the defence against his shot.], [Targets shot down; shots inside the missile's reach; times shot down.],
  [7.3 Offensive BFM], [Staying behind a turning fighter, the heat-seeking missile and the gun.], [Gun tracking time; targets shot down; times shot down.],
  [7.4 Defensive BFM], [Surviving a fighter at your six o'clock and turning the fight round.], [Times shot down; the highest load.],
  [7.5 Against enemy types], [The BVR fight and the head-on pass against a MiG-29A.], [Targets shot down; times shot down.],
  [7.6 At night], [The drone intercept and a BVR fight by night.], [Targets shot down; shots inside the missile's reach.],
  [7.7 Check ride 7], [Everything of phases 1 to 7: BVR, offensive and defensive engagements.], [Every item of phases 1 to 7 the flight gives occasion for.],
)

#idx("Check ride 7")Check ride 7 is flown by day, with no instructor's calls and no switch marks; the #term("notebook") is there as always. One emergency already taught may come, unannounced. A lesson passes when it reaches its end within its time and no item is graded "Unsatisfactory"; the #term("debrief") gives each item's grade (@debrief).
